# J5 — Export the work
# Doc says "continues J4", but the offline demo also persists findings, so
# this runs keylessly: demo → findings exist → is the path from "I have
# findings" to "I have a submittable artifact" discoverable without docs?
# Known risk: export was uncommitted / orphaned in prior audits.
name: Export the work
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
keys: d
wait-for: 90 run completed
snap: demo-findings-ready
keys: Escape
wait: 2
submit: help
wait: 2
snap: help-for-export
ask: Discoverability — from `help`, can an operator find how to export findings without reading docs?
submit: export
wait: 3
snap: export-verb
expect: findings export <path> [format]
ask: Bare `export` — does it print the complete canonical usage, including the required output path?
submit: findings export @ART/report.sarif sarif
wait: 5
snap: export-sarif
expect: report.sarif
ask: Canonical findings export — did it write a SARIF file and say where? (Also try json|csv|markdown-bundle when judging by hand.)
